Add cmd/migrate binary, drop external migrate.exe dependency

The migrations folder stayed the same (SQL files unchanged) but the
runner is now in-tree:

  cmd/
  ├── api/        HTTP server
  ├── migrate/    DB migration runner  ← NEW
  └── seed/       Test data loader

Devs and CI/CD only need Go installed. No more `scoop install migrate`
or `choco install migrate`.

backend/cmd/migrate/main.go:
- Wraps `golang-migrate/v4` (file source + postgres driver).
- Subcommands: up, down [N|all], goto <ver>, version, status, force,
  create. Loads DATABASE_URL from .env.development (skipped for
  `create` so you can scaffold migrations offline).
- `create <name>` auto-picks the next sequence number and writes both
  .up.sql and .down.sql with TODO stubs.
- Forward-slash normalisation so `file://` source works on Windows.

backend/Makefile:
- All `migrate-*` and `seed` targets now use `go run ./cmd/...`.
- New `build-all` target builds all 3 binaries (api / migrate / seed)
  with -ldflags="-s -w".

backend/scripts/migrate.ps1:
- Simplified into a thin wrapper that forwards args to
  `go run ./cmd/migrate`. No more manual .env parsing — cmd/migrate
  does that itself.

CLAUDE.md + backend/migrations/README.md: removed the "install
migrate.exe" instructions; mention the in-tree binary instead.

Verified:
- `go build ./...` → 3 binaries clean.
- `go list ./cmd/...` → api, migrate, seed.
- `go run ./cmd/migrate` (no args) → prints usage.

